@startuml corpus-streaming
' Why a 20 GB dump fits in a laptop: what is resident at each rung of the lazy
' pull chain, and what the *unit of residency* is for each shipped reader.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/corpus-streaming.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/corpus/streaming.md, section "The residency ladder".
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
}
title The residency ladder — what is actually in RAM while streaming a dump

rectangle "**On disk**\nenwiki-latest-pages-articles.xml.bz2 — tens of GB\nnever fully read, never fully decompressed" as disk #546E7A
rectangle "**File**\nstd::fs::File" as fh #546E7A
rectangle "**BzDecoder**\nstreaming bzip2 — one block at a time\n(Burrows-Wheeler; blocks are 100–900 kB)" as bz #546E7A
rectangle "**BufReader**\nwith_capacity(64 KiB)" as buf #546E7A
rectangle "**quick_xml::Reader**\npull parser · read_event_into(&mut buf)\nbuf reused: Vec::with_capacity(8192)" as xml #546E7A

rectangle "**One article**\ncurrent_title + current_text\ncleared at every <page>" as art #1565C0
rectangle "**One Document**\nafter strip_wiki_markup + normalize" as doc #1565C0
rectangle "**That document's sentences**\ntokenizer.sentences(&doc.content).collect::<Vec<_>>()" as sv #1565C0
rectangle "**One sentence**\nyielded to the consumer, then dropped" as one #455A64

disk --> fh : File::open
fh --> bz : path ends in .bz2
bz --> buf
buf --> xml
xml --> art : Event::Text ⇒ push_str
art --> doc : Event::End(</page>)\n⇒ 4 filters ⇒ emit
doc --> sv : flat_map
sv --> one : Iterator::next()

note right of bz
  Decompression is **incremental**: BzDecoder is a Read
  adaptor, so bytes are inflated only as the XML parser
  asks for them. Back-pressure therefore reaches all the
  way down to the disk — nothing runs ahead.
end note

note right of sv
  **The one eager step.** sentences() collects each
  *document's* sentences into a Vec before flattening
  (the borrow of doc.content may not escape the closure).
  Peak residency is therefore *one document's* sentences —
  far less than the corpus, but more than one sentence.
end note

note bottom of doc
  **Unit of residency, per reader**
  · WikipediaReader — one <page> element
  · GutenbergReader — one whole book (read_to_string)
  · PlaintextReader — one whole file (read_to_string)
  ⇒ shard a large plaintext corpus into many files, or use
  LineIterator for true line-at-a-time residency.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Role |
  |<#546E7A> | external I-O / decompression |
  |<#1565C0> | in-memory working set |
  |<#455A64> | consumer |
endlegend
@enduml
